A||||15||fyerstarter||Aftermarket Automatic Shift Knob, will this work with Fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||fyerstarter||06-15-2001||02:10 AM||||Hey all I was thinking about ditching the big gaudy auto ship knob for one of these from JC Whitney. I was wondering is anyone knows it they will work on a fiero? <P> <IMG SRC="http://a235.g.akamai.net/f/235/2654/30d/www.jcwhitney.com/images/imagecache/I18055.gif"> <P>Here is what JCWhitney has to say about the knob:<P><B>For use with automatic transmission single-button shift levers up to 5/8" diameter only. Allen wrench, screws, rubber bushings and instructions included. Approximately 4-1/4"H x 1-1/4" diameter knob. </B><P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-15-2001||03:18 AM||||I don't want to give you a definite 'yes', but I would imagine they'd work.  Unlike the manual shifter, the auto shifter seems to be a universal size (more or less).  Lots of other stock shifter knobs work on it without modification, so I'd think this one would too.  Wish I'd seen it when I still had an auto.  Looks nice.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||06-15-2001||09:45 AM||||Go for it! It's 20+ <I>FREE!!!</I> horsepower, in a Honda!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000003||Mr.Frosty||06-15-2001||10:04 AM||||I'm gonna do it.As I too have a slushbox in mine.I want the carbon fiber one though.I agree that the stock one is "SO" ugly.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000004||fyerstarter||06-15-2001||11:41 AM||||Give it up Mach10. This place is one of the most hypocritical I have ever seen. Where else do you have one thread with someone offering 6" wingstand extensions and everyone drooling and begging for them, and on the very next thread the same people criticising an Eclipse for having a big wing on the back. <P>Get over it. I have seen just as many tacky riced out Fieros as I have Hondas.<P>Thanks to everyone else, I'm looking forward to my 20 hp    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 06-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fyerstarter||06-15-2001||11:55 AM||||On a related topic:   Does anyone know how the heck to get the stock auto ahift knob off?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||06-15-2001||12:18 PM||||Relax man, I wasn't calling you a ricer. Actually, I was thinking of the Honda I saw last week with decals all over the car. To the best of my knowledge, every one of them represented a company that made interior accessories or wheels only.<BR>Fine, it's only good for 10HP  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000007||Mr.Frosty||06-15-2001||12:21 PM||||I've actually made a wood grip stick shift for my auto.It took about a week.I couldn't find a button suitable for the actuator and it also kept rotating in place.I used the stock clip and location to hold it there,but there was no slot to keep it from rotating.It's pretty nice.I sanded it really smooth,stained it,and Varnished the hell out of it.I might try to do another one again soon,but I'm thinking a carbon fiber motif now.Hmmmmm.Too many things to do,not enough free time.Oh yeah I almost forgot,it was a dead ringer for a manual shifter.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled<p>[This message has been edited by Mr.Frosty (edited 06-15-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000008||Phil||06-15-2001||12:21 PM||||There is a small clip on the rear(radio side) of the knob, just pull it out and the knob slides right up and off.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Seanh||06-15-2001||12:24 PM||||That shifter looks cool, I might have to get me one also. How much are they?<P>To take the auto shifter knob off, there is a "U" shaped pin on the back of the shaft. Get a pair of needle nosed plies and pull it out. Just put your finger on the back of the shaft of the shift knob, you'll feel the little cutout for the pin, then just pull it out, and pull the knob off.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mr.Frosty||06-15-2001||12:30 PM||||I don't understand why a lot of these fiero companies that specialize in accessories don't offer a replacement knob similiar to that one?There are hundreds of choices for manual knobs,but nothing in the way of auto knobs.I know there's interest out there for one.For those of us who can't afford a manual tranny swap in our near future,at least it'll look and feel better than that "KnightRider" shift handle.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000011||ThatRickGuy||06-15-2001||12:38 PM||||When someone puts out an 8-ball with the '8' circle being the button, I'll go for it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||06-15-2001||02:18 PM||||I will second that motion  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||saleenfiero||06-15-2001||05:36 PM||||Guys, these knobs fit, I should know, I have one that look just like it on my car.  They are attached (well at least mine is) by three little hex screws digging into the stalk.  Little note:  It you have the 3 hex screw setup, tighten the things TO THE MAX, otherwise it has a tendency to come loose!||||reg||1
Z||000014||theogre||06-15-2001||11:52 PM||||no aftermarket shifters for auto? I've seen a bunch of differant shifters for auto's over the years. GM also has several that will fit other then the original.<P>Once you are sure of a knob....<P>put it on and sinch the screw(s).<BR>then take it back off.<BR>See if the screws left any marks on the stem.<BR>If they did, and you are sure you really like this knob....<BR>file a small groove across the stem where each screw hits. Just a tiny groove will give the screw a much better bite. (If you have an automatic center punch works goood if the screws are pointed. Don't use a regular punch... you could damage the shifter down below by hitting the punch with a hammer.)||||reg||1
Z||000015||fropuff||06-16-2001||12:42 AM||||Originally posted by ThatRickGuy:<BR>"When someone puts out an 8-ball with the '8' circle being the button, I'll go for it."<P>&gt;Well, on Rodney Dickman's site, he has a ball-shaped shifter knob that's used for the auto.  Instead of a button, the entire ball pushes down to shift gears.  It's probably a spring-loaded thing goin on.  I'm sure with little modifications, you could do the same thing with the 8-ball.  <P>||||reg||1
